{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/timeModification","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote\/timemodification"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLNoteV16timeModificationAA07MXLTimeE0VSgvp","roleHeading":"Instance Property","title":"timeModification","symbolKind":"property","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"timeModification","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLTimeModification","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL19MXLTimeModificationV"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The time modification (e.g. for tuplets) applied to this note, if any."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"timeModification","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLTimeModification","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTimeModification","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL19MXLTimeModificationV"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to a nested MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<time-modification>"},{"type":"text","text":" element."}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote"]]},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTimeModification":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltimemodification","title":"MXLTimeModification","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Time modification indicates tuplets, double-note tremolos, and other durational changes. A time-modification"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element shows how the cumulative, sounding effect of tuplets and double-note tremolos compare to the written"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"note type represented by the type and dot elements. Nested tuplets and other notations that use more detailed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"information need both the time-modification and tuplet elements to be represented accurately."}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLTimeModification","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTimeModification","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLTimeModification","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote/timeModification":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote\/timemodification","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"timeModification"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLTimeModification","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL19MXLTimeModificationV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"title":"timeModification","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/timeModification","role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The time modification (e.g. for tuplets) applied to this note, if any."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNote"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNote"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote","role":"symbol","title":"MXLNote","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Notes are the most common type of MusicXML data. The MusicXML format distinguishes between elements used for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sound information and elements used for notation information (e.g., tie is used for sound, tied for notation)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Thus grace notes do not have a duration element. Cue notes have a duration element, as do forward elements,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"but no tie elements. Having these two types of information available can make interchange easier, as some"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"programs handle one type of information more readily than the other."}]}}}